dogecoin.text:
@ProTheDoge Just because something worked doesn't mean it was a good idea. Even if it keeps working, that still doesn't mean it's a good idea.

At least convert 50% of your Dogecoin into #BTC. 

You'd have 500k in BTC guaranteed to go up forever.

@bitcoiner_maxi Plus, he was referring to "everything", not just altcoins.

Take Dogecoin for example. Someone made it as a joke,  never intending to scam anyone. It took a life of its own.

It will trend towards 0 relative to Bitcoin in the long term, but that doesn't make it a scam.
